   "GUILD" accordion friend row was rendering text stacked
   vertically (R / C II / Richie / C-RANK), the "find a hunter"
   input was unstyled default browser white, and the "+ ADD
   FRIEND" button was a default browser button.

   This restoration block surgically re-adds ONLY the non-duel
   rules from the deleted range. Verified against the renderer
   markup in app.js for the outgoing-friend row, the accepted-
   friend row, the friend-add input row, and _friendAvatarHtml.

   Explicitly NOT restored (deliberate omissions):
     - .duel-card / .duel-card--incoming / --outgoing / --active
       and every other .duel-card-* / .duels-* / #ddo-* /
       body.ddo-locked rule — Duels subsystem stays retired
     - .social-btn--gold — zero callers in app.js post-retirement
       (was for the deleted Challenge button); also referenced
       --duels-border-gold / --duels-glow-gold vars that are also
